      "origin_derivations": {
        "H3-1": "Session.new/1 still assigns transport once (literal default QuicHttp3.Transport.Quic). New sites 189-199 (early/resumption queries, extension requirements, uni/kind stream opens, reset_stream_at, datagrams, migrate) call the retained session.transport. The only library session_options producer is the WebTransport backend, which supplies only webtransport limits.",
        "H3-2": "reset_stream_at/4 (200) and migrate/2 (201) call the retained connection/stream ops. HTTP.HTTP3.Resumption creates its shared endpoint with QuicTransport.client/1 from an explicit key projection without :ops, so ops defaults to literal Quic and borrowing still requires ops equality. Quic.reset_stream_at/4 and Quic.migrate/2 route to reviewed Connection operations.",
        "H3-4": "HTTP.HTTP3.Stream.relay_cleanup/2 now creates one library connector callback, fn _deadline -> native_scope(relay) end, only for certified (extended CONNECT with a request lifecycle) exclusive connections with no caller callback or descriptor. Its body calls only Quic.Cleanup.new/1 (Q1) and returns that opaque descriptor. Public option projections still never expose :quic_cleanup. connector_wait/5 is unchanged and moves 333->520.",
        "H3-3_H3-5": "ExQuic wrappers are unchanged; SocketClient still supplies only &handle_http3_event/2."
      },
